    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "Turning Cynical Smirks into Holy Wonder",
      "reflection": "Sarah's journey is one of the most encouraging case studies of grace in all of Scripture. If you read only Genesis 18, Sarah might look like someone who had blown her spiritual chance: she was cynical, she laughed at God's promise, and when confronted by the Almighty, she denied it and lied out of fear: 'I didn’t laugh.' Humanly speaking, you would expect God to say: 'Fine, since you laughed, I will find someone who believes Me.'\n\nYet when you open the New Testament and turn to Hebrews 11—God's Hall of Faith—notice what heaven chose to remember! Verse 11 does not mention her cynical laugh, her scheme with Hagar, or her fear in the tent door. It records: 'By faith, even Sarah herself received power to conceive, and she bore a child when she was past age, since she considered him faithful who had promised.' God filtered her messy human story through the grace of the Cross. He saw the underlying ember of faith that ultimately bowed to His faithfulness.\n\nAnd when the baby boy was placed into ninety-year-old Sarah's wrinkled arms in Genesis 21, she did not cry in bitter memory of her ninety years of barren waiting. She burst into rejoicing laughter: 'God has made laughter for me! Everyone who hears will laugh with me' (Genesis 21:6). God transformed her cynical, bitter laugh into the holy laughter of fulfilled redemption. No matter how many years of waiting, disappointment, or cynical exhaustion you carry, God is able to crown your story with holy wonder."
    },
