    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "Stand Still and Watch Yahweh Fight: Faith at the Edge of the Sea",
      "reflection": "Put yourself in the sandals of the Israelites in Exodus 14. In front of you lies the impassable, deep blue waters of the Red Sea. Behind you, the horizon is thick with the churning dust of six hundred of Pharaoh's elite iron chariots, their bronze armor flashing in the sun, weapons drawn to slaughter or re-enslave you. There are mountains on your left and mountains on your right. Militarily, you are utterly trapped. There is no human way out.\n\nWhat is the natural human reaction? Panic. Accusation. Despair. The people turned on Moses with biting sarcasm: 'Were there no graves in Egypt that you brought us out here to die?' But listen to the towering response of Moses in Exodus 14:13-14: 'Don’t be afraid. Stand still, and see the salvation of Yahweh, which he will work for you today... Yahweh will fight for you, and you shall be still.'\n\nNotice the two commands: **'Stand still'** and **'Go forward'** (v. 15). First, quiet your panicked striving. Stop frantic scheming. Cease trying to engineer your own rescue in human strength. 'Yahweh will fight for you, and you shall be still.' Then, take the next step of obedience straight into the impossible! When Moses stretched his wooden rod over the sea, God didn't merely create a shallow muddy swamp—He sent a wind that carved two colossal walls of water and baked the seabed into bone-dry ground. Where you see a dead end, God sees a highway for His glory. When you are cornered, be still: your Deliverer is already fighting."
    },
