    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "The Smitten Rock and the Sustaining Brothers: Living Water and Collective Prayer",
      "reflection": "Exodus 17 contains two monumental theological pictures of our salvation in Christ. First, look at the water from the rock. The people were dying of thirst and quarreling violently. God told Moses: 'Behold, I will stand before you there on the rock in Horeb. You shall strike the rock, and water will come out of it.' Think of the staggering imagery! God Himself stood upon the rock, and the rod of divine judgment—the same rod that struck the Nile and Egypt—struck the rock! The rock took the blow of judgment, and out of its wounded side poured rivers of living, life-saving water for a rebellious people.\n\nPaul explains the mystery in 1 Corinthians 10:4: 'They drank of that spiritual Rock that followed them: and that Rock was Christ.' Jesus Christ was struck by the rod of divine justice on Calvary. Out of His pierced side flowed the living water of the Holy Spirit to quench our eternal thirst. Grace is not free; it cost the smiting of the Son of God.\n\nThen look at the battle on the hill. Amalek attacked. Down in the valley, Joshua fought with the sword. But the outcome of the battle was decided not by Joshua's blade, but by Moses' uplifted hands holding the rod of God on the mountain! However, Moses was human. His arms grew numb with exhaustion. When his hands dropped, Israel began to lose. What did Aaron and Hur do? They didn't criticize Moses for his weakness. They rolled up a stone for him to sit on, and stood beside him, holding up his trembling arms until sunset! No leader can fight spiritual warfare alone. We need brothers and sisters who will stand beside us, hold up our hands in prayer, and rally under the banner of **Yahweh-Nissi**."
    },
