    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "The Eagles' Wings of Grace Before the Mountain of Law",
      "reflection": "Many people read the Ten Commandments as a cold, rigid list of religious rules designed to squeeze the joy out of life. But look at the divine order in Exodus 19 and 20! Before God gave a single commandment, look at what He said in Exodus 19:4: 'You have seen what I did to the Egyptians, and how I bore you on eagles’ wings, and brought you to myself.' And look at the preface to the Ten Commandments in Exodus 20:2: 'I am Yahweh your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage.'\n\n**Grace always precedes law!** God did not stand on Mount Sinai with thunder and say, 'Keep these ten commandments, and if your score is high enough, I will rescue you from Egypt.' No! He rescued them by the blood of the Lamb, carried them on eagles' wings through the Red Sea, fed them with manna, and *then* said: 'Because you belong to Me, here is how My holy family lives.' The commandments are not the price of redemption; they are the lifestyle of the redeemed.\n\nNotice also the terrifying holiness of God. The smoke ascended like a furnace, the mountain shook, thunder cracked, and the trumpet blast grew louder and louder until every knee in camp buckled. God was instilling a healthy, holy reverence. Moses told them in verse 20: 'Don’t be afraid, for God has come to test you, and that his fear may be before you, that you won’t sin.' There is a massive difference between being scared of God (which drives you away) and having the fear of God (which keeps you from sin and draws you near in reverent awe). Our God is an unapproachable consuming fire, yet in Christ He has invited us to draw near with confidence."
    },
