    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "Consecrated Ears, Hands, and Feet: The Anointing of the High Priest",
      "reflection": "Leviticus 8 and 9 depict the glorious institution of the Aaronic priesthood. Look at what was required before Aaron could step into holy service: First, he had to be **washed with water** (Leviticus 8:6). He could not wash himself; he had to submit to being cleansed by Moses. Then he was clothed in royal garments of 'glory and beauty,' crowned with a gold plate reading 'HOLY TO YAHWEH.'\n\nThen notice the striking ceremony of the blood in verse 23: Moses took the blood of the sacrifice and touched Aaron's **right ear**, his **right thumb**, and his **right big toe**! What a vivid, unforgettable spiritual reality: the priest's ears were consecrated to listen exclusively to God's voice; his hands were consecrated to do holy, uncorrupt work; and his feet were consecrated to walk on righteous, blameless paths! Blood had to cover what he heard, what he did, and where he went.\n\nAnd look at the stunning climax in Leviticus 9:24. When Aaron and Moses followed God's sacrificial pattern to the letter, 'Fire came out from before Yahweh, and consumed the burnt offering on the altar!' God's holy fire fell not to destroy the people, but to consume the substitute sacrifice in their place! The people were so overwhelmed by this divine acceptance that they broke into a spontaneous shout of ecstatic joy and collapsed on their faces. In Jesus Christ, our great High Priest, the fire of God's holiness has consumed the ultimate sacrifice for our sins. We are now a royal priesthood, consecrated to hear His voice, work with clean hands, and walk in His footsteps."
    },
