    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "Look and Live: The Scandal of the Bronze Serpent",
      "reflection": "Look at the shocking complaint of Israel in Numbers 21:5: 'Our soul loathes this worthless bread!' They were describing the supernatural, heavenly manna—the food of angels that had faithfully fed them for nearly forty years—as 'worthless bread!' Contempt for God's daily grace is spiritual poison. When we despise God's gifts, we open ourselves up to the deadly vipers of sin and destruction.\n\nYet look at the remedy God provided. Notice what God did *not* do: The people begged, 'Pray to Yahweh that He take away the serpents.' God did not kill the snakes! God left the snakes in the desert, but He provided a miraculous, all-sufficient **cure**! He told Moses to fashion a bronze serpent and mount it high upon a wooden pole. Think about how scandalous that was: a serpent was the very symbol of the curse! In Genesis 3, the serpent was cursed above all beasts. Why would God use an image of the serpent to heal?\n\nBecause Jesus Christ, who knew no sin, **became a curse for us** (Galatians 3:13, 2 Corinthians 5:21)! In John 3:14-16, Jesus explained to Nicodemus: 'As Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must the Son of Man be lifted up, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life.' On the cross, Jesus took the deadly venom of our sin into His own body. He was lifted up as our substitute.\n\nAnd look at the simplicity of salvation: Moses did not say, 'Climb the pole, manufacture an antidote, or do fifty good deeds.' All a dying, venom-filled Israelite had to do was turn their eyes and **look**! The moment they looked upon the bronze serpent in faith, the poison stopped, the swelling vanished, and they lived! There is life for a look at the crucified Savior. Stop trying to cure your own sin; fix your eyes on Jesus and live!"
    },
