      "who": "Balaam, son of Beor, an internationally renowned Mesopotamian diviner from Pethor on the Euphrates, hired by King Balak of Moab with bags of gold to curse Israel, thwarted by God's sovereign Spirit and his own talking donkey.",
      "whenAndWhere": "The plains of Moab overlooking Israel's camp east of the Jordan, around 1406 BC.",
