    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "Jealous with God's Jealousy: The Fierce Love of Phinehas",
      "reflection": "Numbers 25 presents a shocking, dramatic confrontation at Shittim. Israel had fallen into the trap engineered by Balaam: Moabite and Midianite women enticed Hebrew men into sexual immorality, leading them straight into the worship of Baal of Peor. While a deadly plague was devastating the camp and Moses and the leaders were weeping in brokenhearted repentance before the Tent of Meeting, an arrogant prince of Simeon named Zimri strutted past the crying crowd, openly flaunting a Midianite princess into his tent to commit sexual sin.\n\nWhile others wept in paralyzed helplessness, **Phinehas rose up!** He grabbed a spear, walked into the tent, and executed both Zimri and Cozbi on the spot. Instantly, the plague that had already killed 24,000 people stopped! Notice what God said about Phinehas in verse 11: 'He was jealous with My jealousy among them!' Phinehas felt in his own chest what God was feeling: a blazing, holy hatred of the sin that was destroying God's covenant family.\n\nNotice the breathtaking paradox: Phinehas used a spear to execute judgment, but what covenant did God award him? A **covenant of peace** (*berit shalom*) and an everlasting priesthood! (v. 12-13). Psalm 106:30-31 says: 'Then Phinehas stood up and executed judgment, and so the plague was stopped. That was credited to him for righteousness, to all generations forever!' Real peace is not passive tolerance of evil; real peace is established when sin is decisively put to death. Jesus Christ is the ultimate Phinehas: when our sin threatened to consume us, Jesus took the spear of God's holy justice into His own body on the cross, making atonement for our souls and establishing an everlasting covenant of peace."
    },
