    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "The Audacity of Promised Land Faith: Claiming Your Inheritance",
      "reflection": "Numbers 27 contains one of the most refreshing and inspiring episodes in the entire Pentateuch. Think about where Israel was standing: they were still in the barren plains of Moab, on the eastern side of the Jordan River. Jericho was still heavily fortified. The Canaanite giants were still in their mountain fortresses. Israel did not yet own a single square inch of the Promised Land!\n\nYet here came five unmarried sisters—Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah. Their father had died without leaving sons, which under ancient Near Eastern custom meant his name and property rights would disappear. What did these five women do? Did they complain, despair, or resign themselves to poverty? No! They marched right up to the door of the Tent of Meeting, stood before Moses, High Priest Eleazar, and all the tribal princes, and boldly demanded: 'Give us a possession of land among our father's brothers!' (Numbers 27:4).\n\nNotice the staggering depth of their faith: **they valued God's promised inheritance more than the men who wanted to return to Egypt!** Forty years earlier, ten male leaders had cried: 'We can't take the land!' But these five young women were saying: 'We believe God's promise so thoroughly that we want our deeds of ownership written down before we even cross the river!'\n\nAnd look at God's response in verse 7. God didn't say, 'How dare these women question the patriarchal traditions!' God looked down with delight and declared: 'The daughters of Zelophehad speak right! You shall surely give them their inheritance!' God altered national property law because five women dared to believe His promises. Never be afraid to approach God with bold, respectful faith to claim the spiritual inheritance Christ has purchased for you."
    },
