    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "Underneath Are the Everlasting Arms: The Departure of the Friend of God",
      "reflection": "Deuteronomy 34 is one of the most tender, majestic scenes in all of literature. Moses is 120 years old. He has led this stiff-necked nation for forty years through desert sands, mutinies, and miracles. And now, God calls him to climb Mount Nebo alone. Look at verse 7: 'His eye was not dim, nor his natural vigor diminished.' Moses did not die of sickness, senility, or disease. He climbed that rugged mountain on his own two feet, standing at the summit of Pisgah with God.\n\nLook at what God did for His friend. God stood beside Moses and personally gave him a supernatural panoramic view of the Promised Land—from the snow-capped peak of Mount Hermon in Dan to the blue waters of the Mediterranean, down to the palm trees of Jericho. God showed him the fulfillment of the covenant sworn to Abraham six centuries earlier.\n\nAnd then, look at verse 5-6: 'So Moses the servant of Yahweh died there... according to the word of Yahweh. And He buried him in the valley... but no man knows where his tomb is to this day.' The Hebrew phrase 'according to the word of Yahweh' literally translates as *al-pi Yahweh*—'at the mouth of Yahweh.' Ancient Jewish commentators reverently described it as Moses dying **by the kiss of God**! The Creator of the universe gently closed the eyes of His faithful servant, and God Himself dug his grave and laid him to rest. Why did God hide the grave? Because if fallen humanity knew where Moses was buried, they would have turned his tomb into an idolatrous shrine! God kept Moses' resting place secret, preserving the purity of worship.\n\nAnd notice the final words of Deuteronomy: 'There has not arisen a prophet in Israel like Moses, whom Yahweh knew face to face.' Moses was great, but Deuteronomy ends with a question mark, looking for the ultimate Prophet like Moses whom God promised in Deuteronomy 18:15. Fifteen centuries later, on the Mount of Transfiguration (Matthew 17), Moses finally stepped foot inside the Promised Land! He stood on the holy mountain talking with Jesus Christ—the true and greater Prophet—speaking of the ultimate Exodus Jesus was about to accomplish on the cross! Your earthly finish line is not the end of your story; underneath your life are the everlasting arms."
    },
