    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "Whose Side Is God On? The Sword of the Commander",
      "reflection": "Joshua 5:13-14 records one of the most profound theological course-corrections in Scripture. General Joshua was walking near the massive, double-walled fortress of Jericho. He was studying the ramparts, planning siege strategies. Suddenly, a Man appeared standing in the path with a drawn sword in His hand! Joshua marched up like a courageous soldier and asked the natural human question: 'Are you for us, or for our adversaries?'\n\nListen to the shocking, one-word answer of the heavenly Warrior: **'NO!'** What a staggering answer! Joshua asked an either/or question: Are You on our side or their side? And the Commander answered: 'No!' That one word cuts through all our religious self-centeredness. We are constantly trying to enlist God into our causes, praying: 'Lord, bless my plans, endorse my political party, support my ambition, take my side!' And God looks down from heaven and says: 'No! I did not come to take sides; **I came to take over!**'\n\nNotice who this Figure was: He was not a created angel, for when Joshua fell on his face and worshiped, the Figure received his worship! (When John tried to worship an angel in Revelation 19:10, the angel shouted: 'Don't do it! I am a fellow servant!'). Furthermore, this Commander commanded Joshua: 'Take off your sandals, for the place where you stand is holy ground'—the exact words Yahweh spoke from the burning bush! This was a Christophany: a pre-incarnate appearance of Jesus Christ as the supreme Commander of the armies of heaven.\n\nAnd look at Joshua's response: he didn't argue. He dropped his sword, took off his sandals, fell face-first in the dust, and asked: 'What does my Lord say to His servant?' (v. 14). That is the posture of victory! When you surrender unconditionally to King Jesus, the battle is no longer yours; it is His. And when the battle belongs to God, even the impregnable walls of Jericho will collapse flat before Him."
    },
