    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "The Dirt Floor of the Tent: The Lie That Sin Can Be Private",
      "reflection": "Joshua 7 delivers one of the most sobering moral warnings in the entire Old Testament. Fresh off the miraculous, wall-flattening victory at Jericho, Israel marched up to the modest, small hilltop city of Ai. The spies said: 'Don’t weary all the people; send only two or three thousand men, for the people of Ai are few!' (v. 3). But instead of an easy victory, Israel was routed in humiliated panic, and thirty-six soldiers were killed. Joshua fell on his face in bewildered grief, crying: 'Lord, what will become of Your great Name?'\n\nListen to God's abrupt, thunderous reply: 'Get up! Why have you fallen on your face? Israel has sinned!... There is an accursed thing in your midst!' (vv. 10-13). Notice the principle: **You cannot pray away what you need to repent of!** Joshua was praying, weeping, and fasting, but God said: 'Stop praying and start purifying! As long as there is secret, harbored sin in the camp, My presence cannot fight for you.'\n\nLook at Achan's confession in verse 21. Trace the deadly anatomy of temptation that has snared human souls from Eve in Eden to David in Jerusalem: **'I saw... I coveted... I took... and they are hidden!'** Notice that progression: first the gaze of the eye, then the spark of desire in the heart, then the physical theft with the hand, and finally the desperate cover-up under the dirt floor of the tent! Achan thought: 'Nobody saw me. It's just a coat and some gold buried in the dirt under my sleeping mat. Who does it hurt?'\n\nIt cost the lives of thirty-six Hebrew soldiers! It broke the heart of Joshua! It shattered his own family! **There is no such thing as private sin.** Secret compromise in your life leaks out into your family, your church, and your relationships. Yet notice God's redemptive promise in Hosea 2:15: 'I will give her the Valley of Achor [Trouble] for a door of hope!' When you dig up the secret sin, confess it honestly, and bring it into the light of the cross, the valley of your greatest trouble becomes a door of glorious hope and victory."
    },
