    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "The Audacity of Sun-Stopping Prayer: When Heaven Listens to a Man",
      "reflection": "Look at the extraordinary scene in Joshua 10:12-14. Joshua had marched his men uphill all night from Gilgal. They engaged five combined armies, pursued them down the rocky passes of Beth Horon, and watched God hurl massive, targeted hailstones from heaven. But the sun was sinking rapidly behind the hills of Aijalon, and shadows were lengthening over the valleys. If night fell, the enemy would slip away into the caves and mountain clefts, regroup, and drag out a war that could last for years.\n\nJoshua did something that had never been done in human history: in the sight of all Israel, he looked up into the sky and commanded the celestial bodies: 'Sun, stand still on Gibeon! And you, Moon, in the valley of Aijalon!' (v. 12). Think of the sheer, breathtaking audacity of that prayer! Joshua did not ask for a minor blessing or comfortable provision; he asked the Creator of the universe to suspend the rotation of the earth!\n\nAnd look at verse 14: 'There was no day like that before it or after it, that Yahweh listened to the voice of a man; for Yahweh fought for Israel!' The sun stopped in the middle of the sky and delayed its setting for about a full day! Why did God honor such a wild, impossible prayer? Because Joshua was not praying for selfish vanity, personal fame, or parlor tricks; Joshua was in absolute alignment with the redemptive mission of God! When you are fighting God's battles, doing God's work, and standing for God's covenant, heaven backs your prayers with limitless cosmic authority. Jesus told us in Mark 11:23: 'Whoever says to this mountain, \"Be taken up and cast into the sea,\" and doesn’t doubt in his heart... he will have whatever he says!' Stop praying small, safe, predictable prayers; dare to pray sun-stopping prayers for the advance of God's kingdom!"
    },
