      "who": "Caleb (son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite, of the tribe of Judah), who forty-five years after bringing the good report from Kadesh-barnea, stood before Joshua at age eighty-five with undiminished physical vigor and spiritual zeal, asking for the toughest mountain in Canaan—Hebron, home of the terrifying Anakim giants.",
