      "who": "Joshua, 110 years old, gathering all twelve tribes of Israel to sacred Shechem (between Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal) to rehearse God's sovereign faithfulness from Abraham to Canaan, challenging them to throw away all hidden idols and make an unyielding covenant choice.",
      "whenAndWhere": "Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim, around 1390 BC.",
