    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "As for Me and My House: Drawing the Covenant Line",
      "reflection": "Look at the sacred geography of Joshua 24. Joshua summoned all Israel to **Shechem**. Why Shechem? Because six hundred years earlier in Genesis 12:6-7, Abraham had arrived in Canaan and built his very first altar to Yahweh under the oak of Moreh at Shechem! And forty years earlier in Deuteronomy 27, Moses commanded Israel to stand at Shechem between Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal to recite the blessings and curses. Now, at the end of the conquest, Joshua brings the nation back to the exact same sacred spot to renew their vows.\n\nNotice Joshua's testimony in Joshua 23:14: 'You know in all your hearts and in all your souls that not one thing has failed of all the good things which Yahweh your God spoke concerning you. All have happened to you. Not one thing has failed!' What an extraordinary summary of a lifetime walking with God: **Not one good promise has failed!** God's batting average is 1,000. He keeps every word.\n\nAnd then, Joshua delivers his immortal challenge in Joshua 24:14-15. Notice that Joshua did not force them. He laid out the reality of spiritual warfare: You can serve the old pagan gods your ancestors worshipped in Mesopotamia; you can serve the cultural gods of Egypt; you can serve the local fertility gods of the Amorites; or you can serve Yahweh. But you cannot remain neutral! Indecision is a decision. And then, standing like an unshakeable cedar of Lebanon, 110-year-old Joshua plants his flag in the soil of eternity: **'Choose today whom you will serve; but as for me and my house, we will serve Yahweh!'**\n\nNotice the personal, domestic leadership: 'As for ME and MY HOUSE.' True spiritual leadership begins in your own heart and inside the walls of your own home. Before you try to change a nation or lead a community, establish the rule of Jesus Christ over your own life, your marriage, and your children. Plant your flag today and declare: 'My house belongs to the Lord!'"
    },
