    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "The Left-Handed Deliverer: How God Uses the Unconventional",
      "reflection": "Judges 3:15 contains a delightful, almost humorous divine detail: when Israel cried out under eighteen years of Moabite cruelty, God raised up a deliverer named Ehud, described specifically as **'a left-handed man.'** The name *Benjamin* literally means 'son of my right hand,' yet here was a Benjamite who was left-handed! In the ancient world, left-handedness was viewed as an oddity, a disadvantage, or even a defect. Right-handed soldiers wore their swords on their left hips so they could draw across their bodies. Security guards automatically patted down a visitor's left hip.\n\nEhud took what the world considered a peculiarity and turned it into an instrument of divine deliverance! He forged an eighteen-inch double-edged blade and strapped it to his **right thigh**. When the royal guards patted down his left hip, they found nothing! He walked right into the private roof parlor of the tyrant Eglon.\n\nNotice Ehud's announcement in verse 20: 'I have a message from God for you!' Eglon stood up expecting a flattering oracle, but the message from God was an eighteen-inch blade of divine justice against an oppressor of God's people! Ehud reached with his left hand, struck down the tyrant, escaped through the latrine porch, blew the shofar in the hill country of Ephraim, and led Israel into eighty years of glorious peace—the longest period of rest recorded in the entire Book of Judges!\n\nNotice Psalm 44:3: 'They didn’t get the land in possession by their own sword... but by Your right hand, and Your arm, and the light of Your face!' God loves to use what the world overlooks. God uses left-handed deliverers, humble backgrounds, unconventional skills, and unusual temperaments to accomplish His redemptive purposes. Never despise your unique design or unusual gifts; when surrendered to the King of kings, your perceived differences become the very weapons God uses to set captives free."
    },
