    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "God Calls You According to What His Presence Will Make of You",
      "reflection": "Notice the astonishing contrast between where Gideon was and what God called him. Gideon was not standing on a citadel shouting battle slogans; he was crouched down in a sunken stone pit, beating out sheaves of grain with a wooden rod so Midianite raiders would not spot dust clouds and steal his family's meal. In his own eyes, he was terrified, impoverished, and helpless. Yet the Angel of Yahweh stepped into his winepress and uttered words that seemed almost sarcastic: 'Yahweh is with you, you mighty man of valor!'\n\nGod was not describing Gideon's present emotional state; He was prophesying Gideon's divinely empowered future. When Gideon objected that his family was the poorest and he was the least, God did not argue about his resume. He simply said, 'Surely I will be with you.' \n\nLike Paul learning centuries later that divine power is perfected in human weakness, Gideon had to learn that the calling never depends on the vessel's self-generated strength. God's presence is the strength. What area of your life feels like a hidden winepress today? Stop measuring your adequacy by your natural limitations and listen to the One who sends you."
    },
