    "whatGodIsSaying": {
      "headline": "God Ordains Holy Purpose Before Birth and Quiets Our Panicked Fears",
      "reflection": "In a dark forty-year season when Israel did not even bother crying out to God under Philistine dominion, God initiated deliverance on His own initiative. He did not seek out a political council or an army outpost; He visited a quiet, barren Danite woman in the hills of Zorah. God had already written Samson's days in His book before one of them existed, just as David rejoiced in Psalm 139. Every human life is knit together by God with intentional purpose.\n\nNotice also the beautiful contrast between Manoah and his wife. Manoah was a sincere believer who prayed for parenting guidance, yet when the Angel ascended into heaven inside the altar's flame, Manoah was overwhelmed with superstitious dread: 'We shall surely die, because we have seen God!' Fear blinded his logic.\n\nHis wife, however, possessed profound spiritual equilibrium. She reasoned from God's character and covenant: 'If Yahweh were pleased to kill us, He would not have accepted our offering, nor shown us these promises.' When circumstances terrify you and feelings of impending doom attack your mind, let the calm theology of Manoah's wife steady your soul: God does not invite you to worship Him, accept your sacrifice in Christ, and make eternal promises to you only to abandon you to destruction."
    },
